{"y":2021,"label":"2020–21","coach":"Dan Hurley","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":15,"l":8,"cw":11,"cl":6,"confFinish":"3rd in Big East","finish":"r64","seed":7,"region":"East","apHigh":23,"srs":15.77,"sos":8.59,"ortg":107.8,"drtg":97.0,"pace":66.2,"ppg":71.7,"oppg":64.6,"story":{"headline":"Big East Homecoming, Back in the Dance","text":"UConn's return to the Big East came in an empty Gampel Pavilion as COVID-19 canceled five games and forced four more to be rescheduled. James Bouknight scored a career-high 40 in an overtime loss to No. 9 Creighton, then missed eight games after elbow surgery, but still averaged 18.7 points and made first-team All-Big East. Freshman Adama Sanogo, freshman Andre Jackson Jr. and Rhode Island transfer Tyrese Martin arrived; Isaiah Whaley was Big East Defensive Player of the Year and Tyler Polley was Sixth Man of the Year. UConn finished third, lost a 59–56 Big East semifinal to Creighton, and returned to the NCAA tournament for the first time in five years as a No. 7 seed, falling to Maryland 63–54. Bouknight went 11th in the draft.","moments":[{"date":"2021-03-20","title":"NCAA First Round: L vs Maryland","text":"UConn lost to Maryland 54–63 in the NCAA tournament first round at Mackey Arena, West Lafayette, IN."}],"honors":["Isaiah Whaley – Big East Defensive Player of the Year","Tyler Polley – Big East Sixth Man of the Year","James Bouknight – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020%E2%80%9321_UConn_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Bouknight","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adama_Sanogo"]},"roster":[{"pid":"james-bouknight-1","name":"James Bouknight","num":"2","cls":"SO","pos":"G","ht":"6-5","wt":190,"home":"Brooklyn, NY","hs":"The MacDuffie School","rsci":"72 ( 2019 )","photo":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/mens-college-basketball/players/full/4431712.png","photoStudio":true,"pg":{"g":